TITLE:: ProbeBandAnalyzer
summary:: 16-Band Calibrated Logarithmic Spectral Band Analyzer
categories:: GUI>Visualizers, Live Coding>Telemetry

DESCRIPTION::
ProbeBandAnalyzer displays calibrated ISO octave-band energy (-80 dBFS to 0 dBFS) across 16 fractional frequency bands from 31 Hz to 16 kHz. It features instantaneous peak-hold indicators, smooth decay, segmented level bars, responsive resizing, and broker deduplication.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Open a new standalone window containing the band analyzer.
argument:: server
The Server to monitor. Defaults to link::Classes/Server#*default::.
argument:: busIndex
The audio bus index to monitor. Default: 0.
argument:: theme
A theme name symbol (e.g. \graphite, \phosphor, \ice, \amber, \paper, \monochrome) or link::Classes/ProbeTheme:: instance. Default: \graphite.
returns:: A new ProbeBandAnalyzer instance.

METHOD:: view
Embed the band analyzer into a custom parent link::Classes/View:: or link::Classes/Window::.
argument:: parent
The parent view or window.
argument:: bounds
The link::Classes/Rect:: defining position and dimensions.
argument:: server
The Server to monitor. Defaults to link::Classes/Server#*default::.
argument:: busIndex
The audio bus index to monitor. Default: 0.
argument:: theme
A theme name symbol or link::Classes/ProbeTheme:: instance. Default: \graphite.
returns:: A PB_BandAnalyzerView composite view.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: analyzerView
returns:: The underlying PB_BandAnalyzerView composite view.

METHOD:: window
returns:: The link::Classes/Window:: containing the analyzer.

METHOD:: theme
Get or set the active link::Classes/ProbeTheme::.
argument:: aTheme
A theme name symbol or link::Classes/ProbeTheme:: instance.

METHOD:: fontScale
Get or set the font scaling multiplier (e.g. 1.0, 1.25, 1.5).
argument:: scale
A Float scale factor.

METHOD:: close
Close the analyzer window and release all broker subscriptions.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
s.boot;

// Start live synthesis
x = { Saw.ar(110) + Pulse.ar(440, 0.3) * 0.2 }.play;

// Open Band Analyzer
b = ProbeBandAnalyzer(s, 0, \phosphor);

// Switch themes dynamically
b.theme = \ice;

// Close
b.close;
x.free;
::
